  1+  4010              ; bios.inc -- the BIOS entry points and system variables this book calls by
  2+  4010              ; name (chapter 16). The MSX standard fixes every address: behind each entry
  3+  4010              ; point every MSX BIOS, C-BIOS included, has a JP to a routine of its own.
  4+  4010              ; Call them with page 0 showing the BIOS, as it does when INIT is called.
  5+  4010
  6+  4010              ; entry points
  7+  4010              RDSLT    EQU $000C      ; A = the byte at HL in slot A, a slot ID (chapter 38)
  8+  4010              WRSLT    EQU $0014      ; E to the address HL in slot A
  9+  4010              CALSLT   EQU $001C      ; call the address IX in the slot in IY's high byte
 10+  4010              ENASLT   EQU $0024      ; HL's page shows slot A; the interrupts left off
 11+  4010              DISSCR   EQU $0041      ; the display off
 12+  4010              ENASCR   EQU $0044      ; the display on
 13+  4010              WRTVDP   EQU $0047      ; B to VDP register C
 14+  4010              RDVRM    EQU $004A      ; A = the byte of the VRAM at HL (chapter 19)
 15+  4010              WRTVRM   EQU $004D      ; A to the VRAM at HL
 16+  4010              SETRD    EQU $0050      ; the VDP's address set to HL, to read
 17+  4010              SETWRT   EQU $0053      ; the VDP's address set to HL, to write
 18+  4010              FILVRM   EQU $0056      ; BC bytes of A to the VRAM from HL
 19+  4010              LDIRVM   EQU $005C      ; BC bytes from HL to the VRAM at DE
 20+  4010              CHGMOD   EQU $005F      ; the screen mode in A
 21+  4010              INITXT   EQU $006C      ; text mode, 40 x 24, with the BIOS's tables (chapter 21)
 22+  4010              INIT32   EQU $006F      ; Graphic I, 32 x 24
 23+  4010              INIGRP   EQU $0072      ; Graphic II
 24+  4010              INIMLT   EQU $0075      ; multicolour
 25+  4010              CHSNS    EQU $009C      ; Z if no key waits in the buffer (chapter 34)
 26+  4010              CHGET    EQU $009F      ; wait for a key; A = its code
 27+  4010              CHPUT    EQU $00A2      ; print the character in A
 28+  4010              BEEP     EQU $00C0      ; a beep (C-BIOS: none)
 29+  4010              GTSTCK   EQU $00D5      ; A = 0: the cursor keys; A = their direction, 0-8
 30+  4010              GTTRIG   EQU $00D8      ; A = 0 SPACE, 1-4 a joystick's button: A = $FF if held
 31+  4010              RSLREG   EQU $0138      ; A = port $A8, the primary slots (chapter 38)
 32+  4010              WSLREG   EQU $013B      ; port $A8 = A
 33+  4010              SNSMAT   EQU $0141      ; A = the keys of keyboard row A, 0 = held (chapter 34)
 34+  4010
 35+  4010              ; two bytes of data: the VDP's ports, for programs that ask
